Here my width and height are 1920x1017 instead of 1920x1080 because it's using the maximized client rect size.


So, in short, in DisplayServerWindows::window_set_mode():

```C++
		wd.fullscreen = true;
		wd.maximized = false;
		wd.minimized = false;

		_update_window_style(p_window, false);
```

After _update_window_style() is called, wd.fullscreen is false, because changing the window style triggers signals that set wd.fullscreen to false.

I'm not sure why this doesn't happen all the time, but the logic seems faulty.

Another curiosity: Why is it going through opengl32.dll stuff when I'm using the Vulcan Forward+ renderer?
